{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>You shall not take the name.</b> Since you saw no form, it is not possible to swear except by His name, and even so, <b>you shall not take it in vain, for He will not clear.</b> But one who robs or extorts can clear himself — that can be restored, but this cannot be restored." "<b>In vain.</b> For nothing, as its Targum renders. Do not accustom yourself to take His name for nothing, even in truth, for out of habit you will come to take His name for falsehood, and then you will not be cleared. For HaShem will not clear one who takes His name in vain and for falsehood."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:58.878965971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}